# ---------------------------------
#   ports/base — what the installation medium carries
# ---------------------------------
#
#   <port>...        ports, any number to a line
#   phase <dir>      every port script/phases/<dir>'s list names
#   src <area>       every recipe under src/<area>
#
# The image holds these and their dependency closure over `depends =`, the
# closure not followed into a port ports/buildonly lists unless this file
# names that port itself. Every other port is built, kept in the release's
# binhost and installed from there (`kdos update install`). The closure is
# script/lib/imageset.py's; 70_image/017_stage.sh removes every installed
# package outside it from the staged root the ISO is made of, and
# 087_gates.sh's linkcheck and entrycheck then fail the image when something
# left in it needs a package that went.
#
# A port named here that does not exist fails preflight. A line starting
# with '#' and a blank line are skipped.

